14
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
The Equalizer is a 2014 American vigilante action-thriller film
directed by Antoine Fuqua and written by Richard Wenk.

15
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
It is based on the 1980s TV series of the same title and the
first of three films starring Denzel Washington.

16
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
The cast includes Marton Csokas, Chloë Grace Moretz,
David Harbour, Bill Pullman and Melissa Leo.

17
01:33:30,000 --> 01:33:36,000
Washington plays Robert McCall, a retired Marine and former DIA officer, who reluctantly returns to
action to protect a teenage trafficking victim from the members of the Russian mafia.

18
01:39:00,000 --> 01:39:06,000
Principal photography took place in Massachusetts
from May 2013 to September 2013.

19
01:44:30,000 --> 01:44:36,000
The world premiere for The Equalizer was held at 2014 Toronto International Film Festival
on September 7, 2014, and it was released worldwide on September 26, 2014.

20
01:50:00,000 --> 01:50:06,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics and
grossed $192.3 million worldwide.

21
01:55:30,000 --> 01:55:36,000
The sequels, The Equalizer 2 and The Equalizer 3, were released on
July 20, 2018, and September 1, 2023, respectively.

22
02:01:00,000 --> 02:01:06,000
The film explores themes of assassin, corruption, hitman, call girl, sadism.

23
02:06:30,000 --> 02:06:36,000
The tone is dark and intense.
